{"itchsRODTEPDtlsDTO":null,"notes":[{"noteId":3.33000283E8,"noteName":"Main","noteDetails":[{"notetype":"Main","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"10","noteSerialNo":"1","notes":"<p>(a) The products specified in the headings of this Chapter are to be classified in those headings onlyif grains are present, whether or not in the ear or on the stalk.</p>\n\n<p>(b) This Chapter does not cover grains which have been hulled or otherwise worked. However, rice, husked, milled, polished, glazed, parboiled or broken remains classified in heading 1006. Similarly, quinoa from which the pericarp has been wholly or partly removed in order to separate thesaponin, but which has not undergone any other processes, remains classified in heading 1008.</p>\n","notificationNo":"Notification No. 54/2015-2020","notificationDate":"09/02/2022","noteSection":"II"},{"notetype":"Main","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"10","noteSerialNo":"2","notes":"Heading 1005 does not cover sweet corn (Chapter 7).","notificationNo":"","notificationDate":"","noteSection":"II"}],"noteSectionDetails":[{"notetype":"Main","policyType":"IMPORT","section":"II","noteSerialNo":"1","notes":"In this Section, the term \"pellets\" means products which have been agglomerated either directly by compression or by the addition of a binder in a proportion not exceeding 3 (percent) by weight.","notificationNo":"","notificationDate":""}]},{"noteId":3.33000284E8,"noteName":"Sub-Heading","noteDetails":[{"notetype":"Sub-Heading","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"10","noteSerialNo":"1","notes":"The term \"Durum wheat\" means wheat of the Triticum durum species and the hybrids derived from the inter-specific crossing of Triticum durum which have the same number (28) of chromosomes as that species.","notificationNo":"","notificationDate":"","noteSection":"II"}],"noteSectionDetails":[]},{"noteId":3.33000285E8,"noteName":"Supplementary Notes","noteDetails":[{"notetype":"Supplementary Notes","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"10","noteSerialNo":"1","notes":"<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">For the purposes of tariff items 1006 30 11 and 1006 30 91, &ldquo;Rice, GI recognized&rdquo; refers to the rice varieties defined and recognised by the Geographical Indications (GI) Registry under the Geographical Indications of Goods (Registration and Protection) Act, 1999 (48 of 1999).&rsquo;</span></span></p>\n","notificationNo":"44/2025-26","notificationDate":"15/10/2025","noteSection":"II"}],"noteSectionDetails":[]},{"noteId":3.33000286E8,"noteName":"Policy Condition","noteDetails":[{"notetype":"Policy Condition","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"10","noteSerialNo":"1","notes":"<p>Policy relating to import of wheat by Roller Flour Mills is as follows:</p>\n\n<p>The State Trading Corporation of India Limited (STC) and the Projects Equipments Corporation (P.E.C.) are permitted to import wheat on behalf of Roller Flour Mills subject to the following conditions:-</p>\n\n<p>(i) The import should be for meeting the Roller Flour Mills own requirements for milling purposes and sale of the resultant flour in the domestic market.</p>\n\n<p>(ii) The import contract should be registered by the importing agency with Agricultural and Processed Food Products Export Development Authority (APEDA).</p>\n\n<p>(iii) The imported wheat must be sold to the individual Roller Flour Mills on actual user condition</p>\n","notificationNo":null,"notificationDate":null,"noteSection":"II"},{"notetype":"Policy Condition","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"10","noteSerialNo":"2","notes":"Import permitted for sowing without a licence subject to the new Policy on Seed Development, 1988 and in accordance with import permit granted under Plant Quarantine (Regulation of Import into India) Order, 2003)","notificationNo":"31 (PN)/97-02","notificationDate":"12.08.1997","noteSection":"II"},{"notetype":"Policy Condition","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"10","noteSerialNo":"3","notes":"Import of genetically modified (GM) Rice is Restricted. Import of Rice into India is permitted only if the importer is able to furnish a certificate from the competent Government Authorities from country of export that the exported rice is GM free.","notificationNo":"","notificationDate":"","noteSection":"II"},{"notetype":"Policy Condition","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"10","noteSerialNo":"4","notes":"The existing policy for import of items falling at Exim Codes 1001 19 00 (Durum Wheat: Other) and 1001 99 10 (Other Wheat) shall remain in abeyance till further orders. During this period, import of these items will be allowed freely.","notificationNo":"35","notificationDate":"08.10.2017","noteSection":"II"}],"noteSectionDetails":[]}],"itcCodeClassifications":[{"itcCodeId":null,"unitOfMeasure":null,"itcCode":"1001","itcDescription":"Wheat and meslin.","itchswco":"","impPolicy":"","impItcCodeType":"YES","impCondition":"","expPolicy":null,"expItcCodeType":null,"expCondition":null,"notificationNo":"","notificationDate":""},{"itcCodeId":null,"unitOfMeasure":null,"itcCode":"10011100","itcDescription":"Durum wheat :\n-- Seed","itchswco":" -","impPolicy":"Restricted","impItcCodeType":"YES","impCondition":"Import subject to Policy Condition (2) below.","expPolicy":null,"expItcCodeType":null,"expCondition":null,"notificationNo":"","notificationDate":""},{"itcCodeId":null,"unitOfMeasure":null,"itcCode":"10011900","itcDescription":"Durum wheat :\n-- Other","itchswco":" -","impPolicy":"STE (State Trading Enterprise)","impItcCodeType":"YES","impCondition":"<p style=\"text-align:justify\">Import allowed through FCI subject to Para 2.21 of FTP and Import subject to Policy Condition (4) of this Chapter.</p>\n","expPolicy":null,"expItcCodeType":null,"expCondition":null,"notificationNo":"08/2023","notificationDate":"29/05/2023"},{"itcCodeId":null,"unitOfMeasure":null,"itcCode":"10019100","itcDescription":"Other :\n-- Seed","itchswco":" -","impPolicy":